  "instance_name": "historical_plague_association",
  "label": "Black Death and plague association",
  "description": "The Black Death, which occurred in the 14th century, was one of the deadliest pandemics in human history, killing an estimated 75 to 200 million people in Eurasia and North Africa. The association between rats and the plague is a well-documented historical fact, and the meme references this to imply that rats are a threat to human survival. This historical event is not visible in the image but is essential to understanding the meme's reference to 'European rats in the 15th century'.",
